, paradigm_relatedness\n\nProvide evidence sentence first then score.\n\nProbably JSON? The instruction says return rating... For each subscale give ... first and then... Could be plain text. Safer to output key-value lines.\n\nI'll produce:\n\nid: P2315\neffectiveness_evidence: ...\neffectiveness: 3\netc.\n\nMake sure one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's craft concise sentences.\n\nEffectiveness evidence: The suite verifies logs but does not build the mandated logging capabilities themselves, so it only supports compliance rather than fully solving the logging mandate. Score 3.\n\nApplicability evidence: Verifying that logs capture Article 12 and Annex III events directly addresses the lab's need to meet the record-keeping mandate. Score 4.\n\nAcceptability evidence: Building internal compliance tests is a common, norm-conforming engineering practice that raises no legal or social objections. Score 4.\n\nImplementability evidence: Creating synthetic stress tests and programmatic checks requires dedicated engineering effort and integration into CI, which is feasible but not trivially low cost. Score 3.\n\nOriginality evidence: Compliance unit testing for regulatory logs is an interesting application of standard software testing practice rather than a rare or ingenious invention. Score 2.\n\nParadigm_relatedness evidence: The suite adds a new testing tool and process but keeps compliance framed as logging practice without changing how R&D relates to regulatory obligations. Score 2.\n\nEnsure scores integers.\n\nReturn.\n\n",
