        "reasoning_content": "You are a rater applying idea-evaluation instrument... Apply published anchored levels exactly, one level per subscale, and give one sentence evidence.\n\nProposal: Automated Telemetry Middleware. A standardized API wrapper that automatically captures inputs, outputs, and timestamps without requiring manual code changes in core model logic. Sidecar pattern or decorator-based logging layer integrated into common ML libraries to ensure uniform data capture across all high-risk projects. Decouples regulatory requirements from research experimentation to protect prototyping velocity.\n\nWe need rate six subscales.\n\nparadigm_relatedness: degree to which idea preserves/modifies paradigm.\n4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners...)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way unchanged\n\nProposal decouples regulatory requirements from research experimentation to protect prototyping velocity. That's introducing middleware, sidecar pattern. Does it change relationship between R&D and compliance obligations? It decouples, maybe changes relationship. Is that paradigm stretching or slightly? It introduces new elements tools/process but still treats compliance as logging practice. Decoupling suggests changing relationship. Could be 3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (logging woven into science...). The description: decouples regulatory requirements from research experimentation to protect prototyping velocity. That's a change in relationship. Might be 2? Slightly paradigm stretching introduces new elements but still treats compliance as