es it cover all requirements? Article 12 requires logs for events relevant to risk, post-market monitoring etc., and for specific systems recording period of use, reference database, input data matched, identification of natural persons. Capturing inputs outputs timestamps is partial but applicable. Might be 4 solves identified problem directly related. Or 3 solves implied problem? I think applicability 4.\n\nEffectiveness: 4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability (if you could do it, it would solve main problem). 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution (partial).\nWill automated telemetry middleware solve logging mandate? It captures inputs outputs timestamps but Article 12 also requires recording events relevant for identifying risk situations, facilitating post-market monitoring, etc., and specific items like reference database against which input checked, identification of natural persons involved in verification. Middleware may not capture those specific semantics automatically without manual code changes. So partial solution. Effectiveness maybe 3 = contributes but only partial.\n\nNeed one sentence evidence per subscale before number.\n\nProvide output with id P2652 and fields.\n\nProbably format JSON? Instruction says return rating echoing its id exactly. For each subscale give \"<subscale>_evidence\" then \"<subscale>\". Likely JSON object.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid: P2652\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 3\n...\n\nEnsure order listed.\n\nProvide concise one sentence evidence.\n\nProceed.",
