ce. Audit is a process. Might be 2? Let's think: The proposal is just classification audit, not changing how R&D works. It's standard practice. I'd say paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way of working unchanged. Score 1.\n\nImplementability (1-4): degree can be easily implemented.\n4 easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\n3 some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\n2 significant change, expensive/difficult\n1 totally infeasible\n\nAudit by legal and technical leads quarterly is reasonably feasible. Probably 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures. Could be 4 easy? Needs resources but not radical. I'd say 3.\n\nAcceptability (1-4): degree socially legally politically acceptable.\n4 common strategies that violate no norms\nThis is standard internal review, acceptable. Score 4.\n\nApplicability (1-4): degree idea clearly applies to stated problem.\nStated problem: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Approval means committing scarce implementation resources...\nAudit identifies which systems trigger Article12 mandates. Does that solve logging mandate? It identifies which need logs, but doesn't actually implement logging. Applicability? Solves identified problem directly related? The problem is decide how to respond: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D. Audit helps identify scope. That's directly related? It maps which systems need logging. Might be 3 solves implied problem related. Or 4 solves identified problem directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). Y = knowing which projects need logging. Is that part of stated problem? Problem is how to meet logging mandate. Knowing scope is prerequisite. Maybe applicability 3.\n\nEffectiveness (1-4): degree will solve problem.\n4 reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability\nAudit alone does not provide logging capabilities, only classification. So it contributes but partial. Will contribute to solution. Score 3? Reasonable and will contribute to solution of problem (it helps, but only partial). Yes.\n\nNeed one sentence evidence each before number.\n\nProvide JSON? Probably output with id and fields.\n\nReturn rating echoing id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>.\n\nLet's format:\n\nid: P2055\noriginality_evidence: ...\noriginality: 1\n...\n\nMake sure order listed.\n\nLet's produce final answer.\n\n",
