es to requirement for up-to-date technical documentation per Recital 71 which is part of overall compliance problem. The stated problem is how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D. This addresses adaptation for documentation, which is directly related. Might be 4.\n\nimplementability (1-4):\n4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\n3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\n2 = significant change, or expensive...\nIntegrated system where Git commits trigger updates... Requires tooling, compliance officer review. Reasonably feasible. Probably 3 = some changes, reasonably feasible. Could be 4? Might need development. I'd say 3.\n\nacceptability (1-4):\n4 = common strategies that violate no norms\n3 = somewhat uncommon but does not offend sensibilities\n2 = offends sensibilities somewhat...\nAuto-generated reports reviewed periodically. Seems acceptable. 4.\n\nWe must give one sentence evidence for each rating then score.\n\nOutput format? Probably JSON? It says echo id exactly. For each subscale give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first then \"<subscale>\" integer. Probably return mapping.\n\nLet's produce list.\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: The pipeline embeds compliance documentation into the R&D version control workflow, weaving logging-related obligations into scientific practice rather than treating them as separate overhead.\nparadigm_relatedness: 3\n\noriginality_evidence: Automated sync of Git commits to a regulatory technical file is an interesting DevOps-for-compliance approach but is a fairly familiar tooling pattern in regulated software.\noriginality: 2\n\neffectiveness_evidence: It will keep technical documentation up to date per Recital 71 and support compliance, but it does not directly provide the automatic event logging of system use required by Article 12(1)-(3).\neffectiveness: 3\n\napplicability_evidence: The proposal directly addresses the lab’s need to adapt R&D processes to meet EU AI Act record-keeping and documentation obligations.\napplicability: 4\n\nimplementability_evidence: Building a Git-triggered documentation pipeline requires integration work and periodic compliance review, which is reasonably feasible for an R&D lab.\nimplementability: 3\n\nacceptability_evidence: Automating documentation generation and having compliance officers review it follows common, norm-compliant governance practices.\nacceptability: 4\n\nReturn rating.\n\n",
