neration while still treating compliance as a logging and reporting practice separate from core science. => paradigm_relatedness 2\n\nacceptability_evidence: Automating documentation to meet EU regulatory requirements violates no laws, norms, or sensibilities and is socially acceptable in industry. => acceptability 4\n\nimplementability_evidence: Building a CI/CD trigger that aggregates hyperparameters, datasets and validation results requires some engineering changes but is reasonably feasible for an R&D lab. => implementability 3\n\napplicability_evidence: The pipeline directly addresses the mandate to produce up-to-date technical documentation and audit-ready records required by Recital 71 and Article 12. => applicability 4\n\neffectiveness_evidence: It will reduce manual reporting overhead and flag gaps, contributing to compliance but it does not itself create the mandated automatic event logs for high-risk systems. => effectiveness 3\n\nReturn.\n\n",
