        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "{\"ratings\":[\n{\"id\":\"P2343\",\"paradigm_relatedness_evidence\":\"The gateway embeds Annex III risk classification as a mandatory peer-reviewed gate at prototype inception, linking R&D decisions directly to compliance obligations.\",\"paradigm_relatedness\":3,\"originality_evidence\":\"Risk-based triage with checklists and review gates is a familiar compliance practice applied to AI prototyping rather than a surprising invention.\",\"originality\":2,\"implementability_evidence\":\"Creating a checklist and peer-review gate requires process change and training but uses existing organizational controls and is reasonably feasible.\",\"implementability\":3,\"acceptability_evidence\":\"Early risk classification to limit logging to legally mandated high-risk systems aligns with regulatory intent and standard business practice.\",\"acceptability\":4,\"applicability_evidence\":\"The proposal directly addresses how the lab decides where to apply Article 12 logging by classifying prototypes against Annex III before development.\",\"applicability\":4,\"effectiveness_evidence\":\"Correct triage will focus logging resources on legally required systems and avoid over-engineering, which contributes to but does not by itself implement the mandated automatic logs.\",\"effectiveness\":3}\n]}",
